Are you having problems on shinyapps.io <http://shinyapps.io>, or locally?
This list is specifically for shinyapps.io <http://shinyapps.io>, which is hosted on Linux servers.
If you are having general Shiny questions, you can post to the shiny-discuss group <https://groups.google.com/forum/#!forum/shiny-discuss>.

But it reads as though you are having just a straight issue with R, RODBC, freeTDS and MS SQL locally on a Windows 8 host. I would suggest seeing if you can find a way to verify <http://www.freetds.org/userguide/odbcdiagnose.htm#WITH.UNIXODBC> your installation and configuration of freeTDS outside of R first. When I was trying to figure out connecting to Azure, I found the freeTDS user guide handy, specifically the section on DSN-less connections <http://www.freetds.org/userguide/dsnless.htm>, which was applicable to shinyapps.io <http://shinyapps.io>, but since you are local, you should be able to fully define a DSN to your data source.

Hope that helps get you headed in the right direction. I don't have Windows myself, so if you are still having difficulty and have verified the freeTDS setup outside of R, I would suggest a follow question on a general R list.

Cheers!

